    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "Acts 3:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "The God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified his Servant Jesus, whom you delivered up and denied in the presence of Pilate, when he had determined to release him."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 3:25",
        "textualBasisJa": "You are the children of the prophets, and of the covenant which God made with our fathers, saying to Abraham, ‘All the families of the earth will be blessed through your offspring.’"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 7:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "He said, “Brothers and fathers, listen. The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham when he was in Mesopotamia, before he lived in Haran,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 7:8",
        "textualBasisJa": "He gave him the covenant of circumcision. So Abraham became the father of Isaac, and circumcised him the eighth day. Isaac became the father of Jacob, and Jacob became the father of the twelve patriarchs."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 7:16",
        "textualBasisJa": "and they were brought back to Shechem and laid in the tomb that Abraham bought for a price in silver from the children of Hamor of Shechem."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 7:17",
        "textualBasisJa": "“But as the time of the promise came close which God had sworn to Abraham, the people grew and multiplied in Egypt,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 7:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "‘I am the God of your fathers: the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.’ Moses trembled and dared not look."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 13:26",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Brothers, children of the stock of Abraham, and those among you who fear God, the word of this salvation is sent out to you."
      }
    ],
